From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: implement QCA 8021Q transport and switch VLAN domains

The QCA8K header carries the destination port bitmap on transmit and the
source port number on receive, so a frame to and a frame from the same port
carry different headers. An offload engine that adds and matches one tag
per port cannot carry it. Add a "qca-8021q" tagging protocol on top of
tag_8021q, where each port, or the bridge it forwards in, is one 802.1Q
VLAN in both directions. Register and MIB frames keep the header, behind
the "qca-etype" type, and go to the qca8k handlers as before.

Let a CPU port select "qca-8021q": register tag_8021q, put every port in
VLAN secure mode and keep the header on the CPU ports for management frames
only, behind the same type as "qca-etype", so register access and MIB
autocast stay on Ethernet. The tag_8021q VLANs go through the port VLAN
ops, and bridge join and leave move the ports to and from the bridge VLAN.
Bridges are numbered, since tag_8021q tells them apart by number;
unnumbered, every bridge VLAN decodes as the CPU port and the frame is
dropped. The bridge leaves flooding between bridged ports to the switch, so
broadcast, multicast and unknown unicast flood to every port instead of
only the CPU ports; the port and VLAN members keep the flood inside the
bridge.

A bridge port of one switch tree is a foreign interface to the other trees,
but switchdev hands a VLAN object on a DSA user port to that port alone. On
the RT-AX89X the QCA8337 CPU port then never joins a VLAN that only a PPE
port of the bridge carries, so the QCA8337 drops that VLAN's traffic from
its own ports instead of sending it to the CPU.

Under qca-8021q the switch learns and looks up the addresses of a VLAN-
unaware bridge in the bridge's tag_8021q VLAN. The bridge hands its FDB and
MDB entries over with VID 0, which qca8k puts in VID 1, where no lookup
finds them. The purge of a stale dynamic entry for a station that roamed
from a switch port to a software port of the bridge then misses, and the
switch keeps sending the station's traffic to the old port until the entry
ages out.

qca-8021q needs the CPU port to send every frame with the VLAN tag of its
source port, which the VLAN table asks for. The port egress mode in
PORT_VLAN_CTRL1 overrides the table unless it is "untouched", and qca8k
never sets it. On a GL-B3000 the ports came up in "unmodified" mode, and
the CPU received frames from the user ports without a tag.

